 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "seg-01",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "A new contributor joins our project. We discuss the risk around open source. I document the software license so the team can review it later. If the CONTRIBUTING guide fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the CODEOWNERS file first. At the end of the day, Maria says, \"Thanks for sharing.\" I reply, \"Could you explain your idea?\" The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "tts": "A new contributor joins our project. We discuss the risk around open source. I document the software license so the team can review it later. If the contributing guide fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the code owners file first. At the end of the day, Maria says, \"Thanks for sharing.\" I reply, \"Could you explain your idea?\" The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-01.mp3",
   "zh": "一位新贡献者加入了我们的项目。我们讨论了开源相关的风险。我把软件许可证写成文档，方便团队之后查看。如果贡献指南失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。我建议我们先检查代码所有者文件。一天结束时，Maria说：\"谢谢你的分享。\"我回答：\"你可以解释一下你的想法吗？\"团队就计划达成一致，我记录了决定。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "open source",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "开源，允许他人查看并按许可证使用源代码"
    },
    {
     "w": "software license",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "软件许可证，规定软件可以如何使用和分发"
    },
    {
     "w": "Thanks for sharing.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "谢谢你的分享。"
    },
    {
     "w": "Could you explain your idea?",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "你可以解释一下你的想法吗？"
    },
    {
     "w": "CONTRIBUTING guide",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "贡献指南，说明如何参与项目的文件"
    },
    {
     "w": "CODEOWNERS file",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "代码所有者文件，指定目录或文件的评审负责人"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-02",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "Everyone is welcome here, and we keep the talk respectful. Priya checks with me, \"Please be respectful.\" I answer clearly, \"I appreciate your feedback.\" If the contributor fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the contribution first. The result depends on the contribution guideline, so I check it twice. I explain the pull request template to a new teammate. The day ends with a clear plan for tomorrow.",
   "tts": "Everyone is welcome here, and we keep the talk respectful. Priya checks with me, \"Please be respectful.\" I answer clearly, \"I appreciate your feedback.\" If the contributor fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the contribution first. The result depends on the contribution guideline, so I check it twice. I explain the pull request template to a new teammate. The day ends with a clear plan for tomorrow.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-02.mp3",
   "zh": "这里欢迎每个人，我们让讨论保持尊重。Priya向我确认：\"请保持尊重。\"我清楚地回答：\"感谢你的反馈。\"如果贡献者失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。我建议我们先检查贡献。结果取决于贡献规则，所以我检查了两遍。我向一位新队友解释了拉取请求模板。这一天以一份清晰的明日计划结束。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "contributor",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "贡献者，为项目提供代码或其他帮助的人"
    },
    {
     "w": "contribution",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "贡献，提交给项目的代码、文档或建议"
    },
    {
